        "raw": "Incidentally, you&#39;re aware that Stealth can stack, right? You can use it over several turns and all those +2s add up...so say you use it for three turns in a row without getting hit, you now have a +6 reduction. But if you get hit by anything, even if it&#39;s for a single point of damage, all the Stealth goes away, even the points that aren&#39;t blocked. And if the damage was irreducible, you lose both the hp [i]and[/i] the Stealth. So even worse if you&#39;re Infected and have some Stealth up while Combat Stance is out (not sure why you&#39;d do this...unless it was your first time fighting Rat, I suppose ;)), because then you hit yourself for Infection damage, removing your Stealth, [i]and[/i] then have to punch yourself in the face with your own Combat Stance. For three points of damage, if the Locus is still out!\n",
